# Phase 7 – Project Documentation

## Project Title

**Script-Controlled ACL – Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value**

## 1. Introduction

Access control is an important part of application security. Different users may require access to different records depending on their department, role, or other field values.

This project uses a Script-Controlled Access Control List (ACL) to control record access based on a specified field value.

## 2. Problem Statement

Providing unrestricted access to records can expose information to unauthorized users. Therefore, a mechanism is required to restrict record access according to predefined conditions.

## 3. Proposed Solution

The project uses an ACL with a server-side script. The script checks the required field value and verifies whether the current user is authorized to access the record.

If the condition is satisfied, access is allowed. Otherwise, access is denied.

