## 7. Testing Summary

The system was tested using users with different authorization conditions. Authorized users were able to access the appropriate records, while unauthorized users were restricted.

## 8. Benefits

* Improves record-level security
* Prevents unauthorized access
* Provides automatic access control
* Uses field values to determine access
* Helps protect sensitive organizational information
* Makes access rules easier to manage

## 9. Limitations

* The access logic depends on correctly configured user information and field values.
* Incorrect ACL configuration may result in unexpected access behavior.
* Changes to the data structure may require updates to the script.

## 10. Future Enhancements

The system can be enhanced by:

* Supporting multiple access conditions
* Adding more complex authorization rules
* Providing better access-control reporting
* Extending the solution to additional tables
* Adding automated testing for ACL rules

## 11. Conclusion

The Script-Controlled ACL project provides a method for restricting record access based on field values. By combining ACL configuration with server-side scripting, the system can distinguish between authorized and unauthorized users and control access accordingly.

The project demonstrates how field-based access control can be used to improve the security of records in an organizational system.

